                             hosts, watched files, package installs; re-applies the guards. Events go to vigil's
                             spool (from "sensor"); high ones also to Vals through the alarm bot.
  vigil-ops act              runs the requests vigil queued with vigil-request (path unit), per the policy in
                             /etc/vigil/vigil.toml: auto, confirm (a 4-letter code Vals types back) or off.
  vigil-ops lift GUARD MIN   Vals himself (sudo): lift a guard for MIN minutes without a code.
  vigil-ops status           guards, pending confirmations, blocked IPs.

Runs as root. Standard library only. Written by Claude 2026-10-12 (thread vps-security), TENTATIVE until Vals
reviews it. Everything read from requests, logs and /proc is untrusted data: validated, never executed.
"""
